quare on it is five times the (square) on the radius of circle EFGHK, the radius of circle EFGHK is thus also rational. Hence, its diameter is also rational. And if an equilateral pentagon is inscribed in a circle having a rational diameter then the side of the pentagon is that irrational (straight-line) called minor [Prop. 13.11]. And the side of pentagon EFGHK is (the side) of the icosahedron. Thus, the side of the icosahedron is that irrational (straight-line) called minor.

